{
  "_fixture_note": "SYNTHETIC. No real feeder, tower, relay or radio-coverage data exists for this area; every entity, latency and carrier assignment below is an assumption, labelled data_origin=synthetic throughout. Design principle, declared before measuring outcomes: power feeders and alert backhaul run ALONG arterial corridors, so each is assigned a carrier_corridor_id and is severed when that corridor fails. Carriers are spread across 7 of 14 corridors rather than clustered on 2, and towers have mixed redundancy (some dual-fed, some single-fed) so that a single failure degrades without always breaching. Prior version had 2 towers / 2 relays / 3 links on 2 corridors, which left the alert layer unable to interact with the road layer. Five redundant point-to-point microwave backhaul links (mw_*) carry no corridor, giving every tower a second disjoint path from a command source; without them the backhaul was a tree and 7 of 14 single corridor failures orphaned relays outright, saturating the fixture.",
